Patch-Id: ASTRA-0018
Title: Paint the Astra ground on the browser window before the first stylesheet
Tier: P2
Upstream-Files: browser/base/content/browser.xhtml
Intent: The Windows window is created before the chrome stylesheets apply and paints the platform default white. Astra's ground is part of the window element itself, so the first XUL paint is already the product colour.
Risk: low (a root inline background; the theme and page surfaces still paint over it)
Test: forge lint, forge import --check; startup capture shows no white frame between the pre-XUL skeleton and the first Astra frame
Verified-On: 153.6.0
Removal-Plan: none anticipated
---
diff --git a/browser/base/content/browser.xhtml b/browser/base/content/browser.xhtml
index 661a815519..06bf547b63 100644
--- a/browser/base/content/browser.xhtml
+++ b/browser/base/content/browser.xhtml
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 # file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
 
 <html id="main-window"
+        style="background-color:#1c1b22"
         xmlns:html="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
         xmlns:xul="http://www.mozilla.org/keymaster/gatekeeper/there.is.only.xul"
         xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
